# Security & Secrets

- Never read `*.env`, `*.env.*`, or files that hold secrets.
- Never ask the user to paste secrets into chat.
- Never hardcode credentials, API keys, JWT secrets, KMS keys, or connection passwords.
- Reference env **names** only (e.g. `DATABASE_URL`, `JWT_PRIVATE_KEY`).
- Never log or return passwords, refresh tokens, source IPTV credentials, or raw token values.
- Source credentials at rest use AES-256-GCM ciphertext; the DB never stores clear secrets.
- Prefer Argon2id (or bcrypt cost >= 12) for password hashes when auth is implemented.
